 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "transactions is a list of [payer, payee, amount] rows (party names are strings, payer != payee, amount a positive integer number of cents). Every row moves amount from payer to payee. The end-of-day balance of a party is the total it received minus the total it paid. Level 2: settle all balances with transfers chosen greedily. While some balance is non-zero, take the creditor with the largest positive balance and the debtor with the most negative balance (ties to the smaller name in code-point order), transfer min(credit, -debt) from the debtor to the creditor and record [debtor, creditor, amount]. Return the recorded transfers in order (empty when everything already nets to zero).",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
